{
  "description": "\"A postfix place differs in one observable way, and it follows from evaluation order rather than from scoping\" (spec/execution-model.md:492-499): `:d.k = <value>` resolves its base `:d` as a read before assigning, so inside a procedure that cannot see `d` it raises `ol-var-not-visible` on the BASE, while the same-looking plain write `:d = <value>` silently creates a procedure-local instead. The span is the base `:d`, not the whole place, and `params.procedure` names the boundary as spec/error-model.md:132 requires. The silent half of the contrast is `a-write-first-procedure-silently-shadows-and-still-draws`; the two shapes look identical in source and have opposite outcomes.",
